      "content": "thanks for that. the coverage is at 1.0 now so that should satisfy the automation. \n\none more thing though—the engineering lead is looking at this and says it's a bit \"thin.\" they want a more detailed version that explains the actual flow of a call, like how the headers and tokens work together with the payload and the response.\n\ni know we already hit the 10 terms, so you don't need to just repeat them for the sake of the score, but given that the audit is for \"completeness,\" it would be better if the documentation was a bit more substantial. can you expand this out into a more thorough paragraph or two? just make sure it stays functional and doesn't get too repetitive.",
